      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.286,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "QUADRATIC EQUATIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.105,
            0.898,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "47"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.41,
            0.139,
            0.59,
            0.157
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 4.3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.168,
            0.899,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "**1.** Find the nature of the roots of the following quadratic equations. If the real roots exist, find them:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.219,
            0.339,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "(i) $2x^{2}-3x+5=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.215,
            0.742,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $3x^{2}-4\\sqrt{3}x+4=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.243,
            0.338,
            0.259
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $2x^{2}-6x+3=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.267,
            0.9,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "**2.** Find the values of k for each of the following quadratic equations, so that they have two equal roots."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.309,
            0.341,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "(i) $2x^{2} + kx + 3 = 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.309,
            0.723,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "kx(x - 2) + 6 = 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.334,
            0.898,
            0.369
          ],
          "content": "and the area is $8 0 0 \\: \\mathrm { m } ^ { 2 } ?$ If so, find its length and breadth."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.375,
            0.899,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "**4.** Is the following situation possible? If so, determine their present ages. The sum of the ages of two friends is 20 years. Four years ago, the product of their ages in years was 48."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.436,
            0.9,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "**5.** Is it possible to design a rectangular park of perimeter 80 m and area 400 m<sup>2</sup>? If so, find its length and breadth."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.491,
            0.252,
            0.511
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.5 Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.516,
            0.574,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": "In this chapter, you have studied the following points:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.541,
            0.9,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "$ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ , where a, b, c are real numbers and $a   \\neq   0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.583,
            0.902,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "2. A real number   is said to be a root of the quadratic equation $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ , if $a \\alpha ^ { 2 } + b \\alpha + c = 0$ . The zeroes of the quadratic polynomial $a x ^ { 2 } + b x + c$ and the roots of the quadratic equation $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ are the same."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.643,
            0.9,
            0.68
          ],
          "content": "**3.** If we can factorise $ax^{2}+bx+c,a \\ne 0$ , into a product of two linear factors, then the roots of the quadratic equation $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ can be found by equating each factor to zero."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.685,
            0.899,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": "**4.** Quadratic formula: The roots of a quadratic equation $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ are given by $\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a}$ , provided $b ^ { 2 }   -   4 a c   \\geq   0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.766,
            0.515,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "**5.** A quadratic equation $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$ has"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.791,
            0.53,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": "(i) two distinct real roots, if $b^{2}-4ac>0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.814,
            0.708,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "(ii) two equal roots (i.e., coincident roots), if $b^{2}-4ac=0$ , and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.837,
            0.448,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": "(iii) no real roots, if $b^{2}-4ac<0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.436,
            0.967,
            0.562,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
